            <div xml:id="d1218">

                <pb facs="1219" n="1209" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Executive Secretariat Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Executive Secretary
                        of the National Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Souers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-06-06">June 6, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Pursuant to NSC Action No. 123, October 6, 1948, the following progress report on
                    the implementation of NSC 11/3,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d1218-f1"/> U.S. Naval
                    Forces at Tsingtao, is submitted for the information of the Council:</p>
                <p>The Commander of U.S. Naval Forces, Western Pacific, has reported that all
                    remaining U.S. Naval units were withdrawn from Tsingtao on May 25, 1949. With
                    this action, the phased withdrawal of Naval Forces from Tsingtao has been
                    completed.</p>
                <p>Since there are no longer U.S. Naval Forces stationed at Tsingtao, the action
                    contemplated in NSC 11/3 (Tab A),<anchor n="25" xml:id="d1218-f2"/> coordination
                    of which was assigned to the Secretary of State, may be considered completed
                    and, consequently, no further reports with respect to NSC 11/3 will be made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
